## Symptom\n\nAfter c2c relay disable (parked URL, enabled:false), c2c rename <alias> still phones the parked relay: Relay_rename_rebind.resolve_relay_url (ocaml/relay_rename_rebind.ml:31-36) is env C2C_RELAY_URL -> relay_config_string_field "url" — it never consults Relay_activation.resolve and never checks enabled. B140 wires rebind_sync into rename, so a signed /register POSTs to a relay the operator turned off, and the rename output shows relay_rebind: ok instead of skipped. This is the fourth drifted copy of URL resolution — exactly the failure B301 was written to end, and a B300 contract break.\n\n## Fix direction\n\nDelete the local resolver; route through Relay_activation.url () and map Relay_disabled/Relay_inactive to the existing skipped JSON. Verify with a clean-HOME test: disabled relay.json + rename issues zero HTTP (same netns method as test_relay_activation).\n\n## Evidence\n\nRead-only relay review 2026-09-17 (verified in source by coordinator).